From 561b85acbb7152cc83f3621bb229ea14b94e1389 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 09:27:45 +0000
Subject: net: ethernet: lantiq: add intel_xrx500 netdev/phylink driver with
 CBM TX

Add the network driver: one netdev per LAN port (from the DT port
list), phylink-managed against the internal GPHYs via the GSWIP
MDIO bus.

ndo_open runs the bring-up in the hardware-required order:

 1. TMU egress-port enable for the port's egress port - FIRST; the
    vendor enables the TMU egress port before opening the dequeue
    channel, and reversing this wedges the dequeue handshake.
 2. hdma_port_enable(deq port) - open the port's DMA2TX dequeue
    channel against the CBM DQM staging window - plus the one-shot
    turn_on_DMA_p2p() arming the seeded host-RX bridge.
 3. dp_alloc_port_ext + dp_register_subif (datapath registration,
    which programs the QIDT route via cbm_dp_enable).
 4. TX admit gate open.
 5. phylink_start, then cbm_rx_set_netdev(dev) - the RX engine
    delivers to this netdev from here on. ndo_stop unwinds in
    reverse and unbinds the RX netdev.

The TX path (ndo_start_xmit) enqueues through the CBM rather than
driving a DMA ring directly: linearize/pad the skb, build the
8-byte CPU-to-wire PMAC header, pop a segment from the FSQM
hardware pool (mandatory - the store-forward machinery only binds
payload lengths for pool segments), place header+frame at the fixed
RX offset inside the segment, write the CPU dcache back to DDR
(non-coherent DMA), build the four descriptor words and commit them
with cbm_cpu_enqueue_hw(). On enqueue failure the segment is
returned to the pool. The switch egress port is resolved from the
per-port datapath id; the GSW-L port-5 MAC is activated at link-up
(both the TX and RX gates require the trunk MAC active).

MAC config/link_down are no-ops toward the switch registers: link
state is owned by the hardware MDIO poller, and reprogramming
MAC_CTRL from software fights it.

Also consolidate the composite-module object list into its final
grouping now that all objects exist.

New driver written for this port; the functional reference is the
vendor ltq_eth_drv_xrx500.c from the AVM FRITZ!Box 7560 GPL release
(Linux 4.9.198), which was not ported (its PMAC/DMA model predates
phylink).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
